  "result": "Clean. Summary of the change:\n\n- **`api/queries_user.go`**: Added `CurrentLoginNameAndOrgs`, a GraphQL query that returns the current user's login and the list of organizations they belong to.\n- **`pkg/cmd/repo/create/create.go`**: \n  - `interactiveRepoInfo` now takes the HTTP client and hostname, and after the user enters an un-prefixed repository name, calls a new `interactiveOwner` helper.\n  - `interactiveOwner` fetches the user's login/orgs; if there are no orgs (or the lookup fails), it silently returns no owner, preserving the old un-prefixed behavior. Otherwise it shows a `Select` prompt \"Repository owner\" listing the personal account (default) plus each organization; picking an org prefixes the repo name with `org/`, picking the personal account leaves it unprefixed.\n  - Updated both call sites (`createFromScratch`, `createFromLocal`) to pass `httpClient`/`host` through.\n\nVerified with `go build ./...`, `go vet`, and `go test ./pkg/cmd/repo/create/... ./api/...` \u2014 all pass, existing interactive tests unaffected since the org lookup gracefully no-ops when unstubbed/failing.",
